G4864.b:
⟪συν-αγωγή⟫, -ῆς, ἡ
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨עֵדָה⁩, also for ⁨קהל⁩, etc. ;] prop., ⟪a bringing together⟫;
⟪1.⟫ of things,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a gathering in⟫ of harvest;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪a collection⟫ of money.
⟪2.⟫ Of persons,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a collecting, assembling⟫ (Polyb.);
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪an assembly⟫ (MM, xxiv; Deiss., LAE, 101 ff.): ⟦Revelation 2:9|Re 2:9⟧ ⟦Revelation 3:9|3:9⟧; esp. of a Jewish religious assembly, ⟪a synagogue⟫: ⟦Luke 12:11|Lk 12:11⟧, ⟦Acts 9:2|Ac 9:2⟧, al.; of a Christian assembly, ⟦James 2:2|Ja 2:2⟧. By meton., of the building in which the assembly is held, ⟪a synagogue⟫: ⟦Matthew 10:17|Mt 10:17⟧, ⟦Mark 1:21|Mk 1:21⟧, al. (cf. Cremer, s.v. ἐκκλησία)
SYN.: ἐκκλησία (q.v.)

G4820.b:
⟪συν-βάλλω⟫
(Rec. συμ-), [in LXX: ⟦2 Chronicles 25:19|II Ch 25:19⟧ (⁨גּרה⁩ hith.), ⟦Isaiah 46:6|Is 46:6⟧ (⁨זוּל⁩), ⟦Jeremiah 43:3|Je 50 (43):3⟧ (⁨סוּת⁩ hi.), Wi 5:8, al. ;] ⟪to throw together⟫, hence,
⟪(a)⟫ of speech (seq. λόγους, Eur., al.), ⟪to discuss, confer⟫ (sc. λόγους): c. dat. pers., ⟦Luke 11:53|Lk 11:53⟧, WH, mg., ⟦Acts 17:18|Ac 17:18⟧; seq. πρὸς ἀλλήλους, ⟦Acts 4:15|Ac 4:15⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to reflect, consider, ponder⟫: ἐν τ. καρδίᾳ, ⟦Luke 2:19|Lk 2:19⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪to meet with, fall in with⟫: ⟦Acts 20:14|Ac 20:14⟧; in hostile sense, εἰς πόλεμον, c. dat. (εἰς μάχην, Polyb.), ⟦Luke 14:31|Lk 14:31⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ mid., ⟪to contribute⟫ (Polyb., al.; cf. MM, xxiv): ⟦Acts 18:27|Ac 18:27⟧.†
